// Go workspace for in-repo development across zeroid's published
// modules. When you run `go build` or `go test` from anywhere inside the
// repo, Go reads this file and treats all modules as one workspace
// — local code in ./pkg/authjwt, ./pkg/dpop and ./pkg/jwks is used directly,
// regardless of what versions zeroid/go.mod's require directives
// declare. This lets zeroid/go.mod reference real published subpackage
// versions (required for downstream `go get` resolution) without
// breaking the in-repo dev loop.
//
// Each nested module also has `replace => ./pkg/...` in zeroid/go.mod
// so GOWORK=off paths (Docker layer cache `go mod download`, some CI)
// use local source. Downstream consumers IGNORE those replaces — Go
// does not apply replace directives from dependency modules — so the
// require pins are what the proxy serves and must be real tags.
//
// Releases: see RELEASING.md. All modules release in LOCKSTEP at one
// version, tagged at one commit, so `make release-prep VERSION=vX.Y.Z`
// is the only version ceremony.

go 1.27.0

use (
	.
	./pkg/authjwt
	./pkg/dpop
	./pkg/jwks
)
